'''Fiesta Inn''' is a Mexican business-class [[hotel]] brand.<ref>[http://www.tripadvisor.com/Hotel_Review-g150800-d281704-Reviews-Fiesta_Inn_Centro_Historico-Mexico_City_Central_Mexico_and_Gulf_Coast.html Fiesta Inn Centro Historico (Mexico City) - Hotel Reviews - TripAdvisor<!-- Bot generated title -->]</ref><ref>[http://www.expedia.com/Guadalajara-Hotels-Fiesta-Inn-Guadalajara-Expo.h198142.Hotel-Information# Fiesta Inn Guadalajara Expo (Guadalajara, Mexico) | Expedia<!-- Bot generated title -->]</ref>  It is owned by [[Grupo Posadas|Grupo Posadas, Inc.]], which also owns other Mexican hotel brands, including the upscale [[Fiesta Americana]] and [[Fiesta Americana Grand]], ultra-luxury [[Live Aqua]], One, and the eco-tourist Explorean.  There are 61 hotels operated under this brand throughout the country.

== Recognition ==
Many Fiesta Inn hotels have received recognition for their high quality, both by government and independent organizations.  A recent example or government recognition is the [[Distintivo H]] award awarded by the Mexican federal [[Secretariat of Tourism]] to the Celaya Fiesta Inn in 2009,<ref>{{in lang|es}} [http://archivo.periodico.am/nota.aspx?id=329175 Periódico a.m. - Recibe el Fiesta Inn Distintivo H<!-- Bot generated title -->] {{Webarchive|url=https://archive.today/20130403180840/http://archivo.periodico.am/nota.aspx?id=329175 |date=2013-04-03 }}</ref> as well as a Fiesta Inn in the State of [[Querétaro]] which received that same award in 2010.<ref>[http://www.queretaro.gob.mx/documentos_interna1.aspx?q=vUYGbsxLnlhg8KRn8eaNGanzAL49/UcC Entrega de Distintivo H al Hotel Fiesta Inn<!-- Bot generated title -->]</ref>  As for non-governmental evaluators, TripAdvisor ranks the Fiesta Inn in [[Mexicali]] as the leading hotel in that city.<ref>[http://www.tripadvisor.com/Hotel_Review-g154247-d530492-Reviews-Fiesta_Inn_Mexicali-Mexicali_Baja_California.html Fiesta Inn Mexicali (Mexico) - Hotel Reviews - TripAdvisor<!-- Bot generated title -->]</ref>  The Fiesta Inn Tollucan in [[Toluca]] has received a rating of 3 diamonds from the [[American Automobile Association]].

== History ==

Fiesta Inn was launched as the business traveler oriented brand of Grupo Posadas in 1982.<ref>{{in lang|es}} [http://www.posadas.com/portal/landingpage/WebsitePosadas/esp_nuestra_empresa.htm Grupo Posadas<!-- Bot generated title -->] {{Webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130107045200/http://www.posadas.com/portal/landingpage/WebsitePosadas/esp_nuestra_empresa.htm |date=2013-01-07 }}</ref>  The Fiesta Inn in Mexico City was damaged during protests in connection with the 2012 inauguration of Mexico's new president.<ref>[http://latino.foxnews.com/latino/news/2012/12/07/random-detentions-as-mexico-swore-in-president-enrique-pena-nieto-commission/ Random Detentions of Protesters as Mexico Swore in President Peña Nieto, Commission Says | Fox News Latino<!-- Bot generated title -->]</ref>  On December 21, 2012, [[Standard & Poor's]] Rating Services raised the rating of the global scale corporate credit rating of the parent company to 'B' and stated that several of the parent companies brands, including Fiesta Inn, are "well-recognized in the country [Mexico]."<ref>[https://archive.today/20130216181153/http://www.reuters.com/article/2012/12/21/idUSWNB259420121221 TEXT - S&P raises Grupo Posadas ratings | Reuters<!-- Bot generated title -->]</ref>

News reports are stating that the parent company is considering building a new Fiesta Inn in [[Silao]], [[Guanajuato]].<ref>{{in lang|es}} [http://www.periodico.am/leon/vieneonehotelsofiestainnapuertointerior-76078.html Traen dos hoteles Posadas y Marriot - León<!-- Bot generated title -->] {{Webarchive|url=https://archive.today/20130219095805/http://www.periodico.am/leon/vieneonehotelsofiestainnapuertointerior-76078.html |date=2013-02-19 }}</ref>

In October 2021, Grupo Posadas filed for [[Chapter 11 bankruptcy]] protection in the US in an effort to stabilize its financial challenges and problems further escalated by the [[COVID-19 pandemic]].<ref>{{Cite web|url= https://www.reuters.com/legal/transactional/mexican-hotel-chain-grupo-posadas-files-chapter-11-us-2021-10-26/ |title=Mexican hotel chain Grupo Posadas files for Chapter 11 in U.S.|date=October 26, 2021|access-date=August 13, 2025|website=Reuters|language=en}}</ref>

